# A here-document whose FIRST body line is `#notacomment` (POSIX §2.7.4). A here-doc
# body is DATA, never shell, so a leading `#` is literal content, NOT a comment. The
# body must begin at the byte after the command line's terminating newline with no
# trivia skipping. (Pre-fix the line-level drain ran under the command line's extras,
# whose Comment extra would consume `#notacomment` as a Comment node and drop it from
# the body.) Here the `#notacomment\n` line is one HeredocContentLine and NO Comment
# node appears inside the heredoc body.
<<<cmd
printf 'cat <<EOF\n#notacomment\nEOF\n' | "$PP" run std.shell --input - --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
out-absent Comment
out-count 1 HeredocBody [
out-count 1 HeredocContentLine
out-order HeredocContentLine [10-23] [1,0] ~ end: HeredocDelimLine
